# SDD Integration — OpenSpec (core)

[OpenSpec](https://github.com/Fission-AI/OpenSpec) is the only SDD framework supported by this project. Do not generate or update artifacts for other SDD frameworks (Memory Bank, Spec Kit, TaskMaster, …), even if their folders or MCP servers happen to be present.

## Load by phase — read only what the phase needs

This file is the core: routing, the DoD contract in brief, question discipline at a glance, subagent ownership, archive. Phase details live in two companion rules; load the one for the current phase, once per session (an already loaded rule is not re-read when the phase or turn changes):

| Phase | Also load | Owns |
|---|---|---|
| Propose, `/opsx:update`, `/opsx:explore` that ends in artifacts | [`sdd-propose.mdc`](sdd-propose.mdc) | DoD authoring (specify completion before apply), spec size triage, pre-author MCP checks, Context sources block, propose clarification gate, Open Questions |
| Apply | [`sdd-apply.mdc`](sdd-apply.mdc) | reuse check before a new helper, apply until DoD is satisfied, DoD reconciliation, preflight round, banned apply-time questions, opening template |
| Archive, `/opsx:sync` | this file; `sdd-apply.mdc → Apply until DoD is satisfied` only to check evidence | archive readiness below |

